WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.490 --> 00:00:01.570
Your app is running.

2
00:00:01.590 --> 00:00:03.180
But is it working?

3
00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:05.392
A process can be alive and stuck.

4
00:00:05.412 --> 00:00:08.465
Kubernetes cannot know, unless you tell it.

5
00:00:08.485 --> 00:00:13.540
This port has three tools: probes, resource limits, and autoscaling.

6
00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:16.025
First: let the cluster ask your app.

7
00:00:16.045 --> 00:00:18.150
Readiness asks: can you serve now?

8
00:00:18.170 --> 00:00:20.610
If not, the pod gets no traffic.

9
00:00:20.630 --> 00:00:22.360
Liveness asks: are you stuck?

10
00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:24.845
If yes, the container restarts.

11
00:00:24.865 --> 00:00:27.483
Never check the database in a liveness probe.

12
00:00:27.503 --> 00:00:31.045
One slow database restarts every pod.

13
00:00:31.065 --> 00:00:33.330
Second: how much may a pod take?

14
00:00:33.350 --> 00:00:35.455
A request reserves capacity.

15
00:00:35.475 --> 00:00:38.165
The scheduler uses it to place the pod.

16
00:00:38.185 --> 00:00:40.690
Over the processor limit, you are slowed down.

17
00:00:40.710 --> 00:00:43.615
Over the memory limit, you are killed.

18
00:00:43.635 --> 00:00:45.550
Third: follow the load.

19
00:00:45.570 --> 00:00:50.285
An autoscaler watches the processor use, and adds or removes pods.

20
00:00:50.305 --> 00:00:51.822
No room for the new pods?

21
00:00:51.842 --> 00:00:54.910
A node autoscaler adds machines.

22
00:00:54.930 --> 00:00:56.745
Quick recap of health.

23
00:00:56.765 --> 00:00:58.232
Readiness gates traffic.

24
00:00:58.252 --> 00:00:59.495
Liveness restarts.

25
00:00:59.515 --> 00:01:01.980
And memory over the limit is killed.

26
00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:05.100
Now start the first lesson below.
